le in v4.8.dev2.official [7220d456d]\n- Not Reproducible in v4.7.2.stable.mono.official [ed1daf0bf]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev (5ec4857b3) - Windows 10 (build 17134) - Multi-window, 1 monitor (2560x1080 @ 60.00 Hz) - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1070 (NVIDIA; 31.0.15.3141) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-7700 CPU @ 3.60GHz (8 threads) - 23.92 GiB memory - WASAPI (96000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\n4.8 is showing really bad artifacts on materials that use normal maps. This is happening with the assets from the [Bistro-DEMO-tweked](https://github.com/Jamsers/Bistro-Demo-Tweaked) but not with the default cube MeshInstance3D. \n\nThis regression started happening in 4.8-dev3.\n\n<img width=\"663\" height=\"530\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/54d06cf5-0ceb-40ea-98d0-bde7aaab6bb3\" />\n\nAlso, not sure if it is related, but disabling Create Shadow Mask on import also completely breaks everything.\nTho the broken shadow fixes itself on project restart. The normal map artifacts continues the same.\n\n<img width=\"911\" height=\"559\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2db5d3e5-e844-460b-bc5a-334837c03d13\" />\n\n\n---\n\n**Enabling SSR, SSAO, SSIL seems to fix these artifact.** \n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/970c6256-8101-41c3-9c3d-2b146d72e49c\n\n\n---\n\nHere is a video showing the bug\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1d44db64-dc3c-4cfc-a918-5fdbbc1a5d6b\n\nAnd how it was working on 4.7\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/338dda8a-c380-48d5-b78f-5cadb9863978\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSteps:\n1. Import a custom mesh from the Distro-DEMO-Tweked\n2. Add an override material material and enable Normal Map\n\nResult: Really bad artifacts\nExpected: Normal material display\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[BAD Artifacts normals MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31603296/BAD.Artifacts.normals.MRP.zip)","cl